-- Schema 1 -> 2: adds `scan_usage`.
--
-- The first migration this database has ever had, and it exists because 1.0 is on
-- Play. Until now every schema change landed before anyone had a copy, so the .sq
-- files alone were enough: SQLDelight builds the schema from them on a fresh
-- install. An existing install is different — its `user_version` is 1, and a table
-- that only exists in a .sq file is a table that phone has never created. The first
-- query against it would fail with "no such table".
--
-- So every schema change from here on needs a file like this one as well as the
-- edit to the .sq. The number is the version being migrated *from*: this one takes
-- a version-1 database to version 2, and `OdoDatabase.Schema.version` becomes 2
-- because of it. The statements below must match ScanUsage.sq exactly — the .sq is
-- what a fresh install creates, this is what an upgrade runs, and they are two
-- descriptions of one table.
CREATE TABLE scan_usage (
    month      TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    scan_count INTEGER NOT NULL
);
